From 52fb72537eadda963a2c2a7d2cca1f75affeea1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:42:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] Support building with the Mac OS X 10.5 SDK

Untested, 10.5 has never been tried. Everything here is conditional on
MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MAX_ALLOWED < 1060 (COCOA_LEOPARD in the Cocoa code,
UPP_MACH_SEMAPHORE in Core), a build with the 10.6 SDK is not changed,
with the exception of two calls that were moved into helper functions.

Core:
- Semaphore: Grand Central Dispatch is 10.6+, and unnamed POSIX
  semaphores are not implemented in Darwin. Use Mach semaphores.

Cocoa, declarations missing in the 10.5 SDK:
- NSApplicationDelegate, NSWindowDelegate and NSMenuDelegate are
  informal protocols there; declare empty formal ones.
- NSPasteboardTypeString/RTF/PNG, NSImageNameCaution.
- NSMoviesDirectory, NSMusicDirectory, NSPicturesDirectory.
- kCTFontURLAttribute: get the font file through ATS.
- NSTextInputContext: use NSInputManager.

Cocoa, methods missing in 10.5:
- -[NSImage initWithCGImage:size:] -> NSBitmapImageRep (CocoNSImage)
- +[NSWindow windowNumbersWithOptions:] -> NSWindowList
- -[NSPasteboard clearContents], writeObjects:,
  readObjectsForClasses:options: -> declareTypes:owner:,
  setPropertyList:forType:, propertyListForType:, URLFromPasteboard:
- -[NSApp setActivationPolicy:] -> TransformProcessType
- +[NSEvent doubleClickInterval], keyRepeatDelay, keyRepeatInterval
  -> user defaults
- -[NSMenu popUpMenuPositioningItem:atLocation:inView:]
  -> +popUpContextMenu:withEvent:forView: with a synthesized event
- -[NSApp setHelpMenu:], -[NSWindow setStyleMask:]: left out
- +[NSCursor operationNotAllowedCursor] exists in 10.5 but is not
  declared in its SDK; call it through the selector.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
